        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بھولنا (bhūlnā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bhull, \"err, forget\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 9538)."
            }
